  "decisions": [
    "Keep the basic and nonbasic header populations separate. All15 dual headers need a neutral L-source overlay; their colored source headers must not drive per-color fits.",
    "Each colored land header fit uses only its three basics. Six missing dual observations are intentional source-role exclusions, not successful zero-error samples.",
    "The15 dual neutral-header targets share one source model from all three generic-land controls; the three generic-land full plates retain their own header observations.",
    "Do not apply the proposed white frame transform: mean distance worsens from3.38 to4.16. Retain identity until a better justified model wins native validation.",
    "Fixed side frame patches mix the common brown land texture and colored rails. Inspect that mixture and the shared-source pixels before choosing global versus per-color frame corrections.",
    "Native masks, colored rails, geometry, black point, contrast and final native replay remain open. No production land default or completed checklist is enabled."
  ]
}
